{"content":[{"c":["PELATIAH"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Hananiah’s son, in a list of King Solomon’s descendants (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.3.21","r":"1Chr.3.21","rawR":"1Chr.3.21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.3.21","value":"1Chr.3.21"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 3:21"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Military leader among the Simeonites who helped destroy an Amalekite remnant at Mt Seir during Hezekiah’s reign (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.4.42","r":"1Chr.4.42","rawR":"1Chr.4.42","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.4.42","value":"1Chr.4.42"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 4:42"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["3. Political leader who signed Ezra’s covenant of faithfulness to God with Nehemiah and others after the exile (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.10.22","r":"Neh.10.22","rawR":"Neh.10.22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.10.22","value":"Neh.10.22"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 10:22"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["4. Benaiah’s son and one of the two princes seen by Ezekiel in a vision of judgment, identified by the Spirit of the Lord as one who devises wickedness and gives wicked counsel in the city (",{"href":"?bref=Ezek.11.1-2,13","r":"Ezek.11.1-2,13","rawR":"Ezek.11.1-2,13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezek.11.1-2,13","value":"Ezek.11.1-2,13"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ez 11:1-2, 13"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Pelatiah","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"1 Chr 3:21","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.3.21","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.3.21","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.3.21"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 4:42","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.4.42","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.4.42","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.4.42"},{"anchorText":"Neh 10:22","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.10.22","rawQueryValu